1162+ CC49 C9                           RET
1163+ CC4A
1164+ CC4A              ; Read a FAT sector into RawPak_FatBuf (resident in Core / slot 1). Keeps the
1165+ CC4A              ; FAT-chain walk from clobbering the slot-2 data buffer (#8000) that callers
1166+ CC4A              ; fill with directory/file sectors. HL:DE = LBA on entry.
1167+ CC4A              RawPak_ReadFatSector:
1168+ CC4A DD 21 CB CE                  LD   IX, RawPak_FatBuf
1169+ CC4E C3 E4 C2                     JP   sd_read_sector
1170+ CC51
1171+ CC51              ; --- Sector-run table (handles both contiguous AND fragmented PAK) ----------
1172+ CC51              ; Requirement: read the PAK whether it is one contiguous run or fragmented.
1173+ CC51              ; The old fast path assumed contiguity (LBA = PakLba + N) — true on a freshly
1174+ CC51              ; built image, but a fragmented file would read the wrong sectors on the upper
1175+ CC51              ; levels. Instead we walk the FAT chain once at open time and record the file as
1176+ CC51              ; a list of extents (runs) {LBA, len_sectors}: a contiguous file collapses to a
1177+ CC51              ; single run, a fragmented one to several. RawPak_ReadOneLogicalIX then maps a
1178+ CC51              ; logical sector to a physical LBA via this table — O(runs), no per-read FAT
1179+ CC51              ; walk, so a section still reads in one SD burst (no FT.WriteMem interleaving).
1180+ CC51
1181+ CC51              RAWPAK_RUN_MAX  EQU 128                ; max extents (128 * 6 = 768 B). Overflow -> open fails -> L1 fallback.
1182+ CC51
1183+ CC51              ; RawPak_BuildRunTable — walk the chain from RawPak_FileStartClus, fill
1184+ CC51              ; RawPak_RunTable / RawPak_RunCount. CurSecInClus must be 0 (set by Seek0).
1185+ CC51              ; Out: CF=1 ok; CF=0 on run-table overflow (heavily fragmented) or SD error.
1186+ CC51              ;
1187+ CC51              ; Scans the FAT *directly*, not via RawPak_FatNext: it keeps a pointer into
1188+ CC51              ; RawPak_FatBuf and reads consecutive 4-byte FAT entries, only recomputing the
1189+ CC51              ; FAT-sector LBA (the expensive cluster>>7) when it crosses a 128-entry sector
1190+ CC51              ; boundary or follows a non-sequential link. A contiguous PAK (the common case)
1191+ CC51              ; then costs ~ one FAT-sector read per 128 clusters and a tight inner loop —
1192+ CC51              ; instead of a full cluster>>7 + 32-bit shift chain per cluster.
1193+ CC51              RawPak_BuildRunTable:
1194+ CC51 21 BF CE                     LD   HL, RawPak_FileStartClus
1195+ CC54 11 C3 CE                     LD   DE, RawPak_CurClus
1196+ CC57 CD FF CD                     CALL RawPak_Copy32
1197+ CC5A AF                           XOR  A
1198+ CC5B 32 24 CE                     LD   (RawPak_CurSecInClus), A
1199+ CC5E                              ; --- first run: LBA = LBA(FileStartClus), len starts at 0 ---
1200+ CC5E DD 21 D6 D0                  LD   IX, RawPak_RunTable
1201+ CC62 CD 28 CB                     CALL RawPak_CurrentLbaRegs      ; HL = LBA lo16, DE = LBA hi16
1202+ CC65 DD 75 00                     LD   (IX + 0), L
1203+ CC68 DD 74 01                     LD   (IX + 1), H
